\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.2}{\ignorespaces Which training sequences each sound candidate accepts. Top: share of the training visits per sequence (logarithmic scale), from the most to the least frequent sequence. Middle: number of stops of each sequence. Bottom: one row per net; a coloured cell means that the net accepts the complete sequence. The six most frequent sequences cover 88.5\,\% of the visits, so a net that accepts few sequences can still fit most visits.}}{68}{figure.caption.42}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:res_e1_variant_coverage}{{6.2}{68}{Which training sequences each sound candidate accepts. Top: share of the training visits per sequence (logarithmic scale), from the most to the least frequent sequence. Middle: number of stops of each sequence. Bottom: one row per net; a coloured cell means that the net accepts the complete sequence. The six most frequent sequences cover 88.5\,\% of the visits, so a net that accepts few sequences can still fit most visits}{figure.caption.42}{}}
